{
    "title": "Texas Outdoor Annual",
    "description": "The Texas Outdoor Annual contains hunting, fishing, and boating regulations, all in one app.\r\n\r\nHunting:\r\n- Hunting season dates & limits for your county\r\n- Seasons and bag limits for all game animals\r\n- Means and methods restrictions\r\n- Game tagging instructions\r\n- Latest hunting news from TPWD*\r\n- Links to report your hunt harvest\r\n\r\nFishing\r\n- Statewide bag and length limits\r\n- Exceptions to statewide limits by water body\r\n- Places to fish nearby (over 1,000 locations)\r\n- Fish identification\r\n- Weekly fishing reports*\r\n- Latest fishing news from TPWD*\r\n- Links to report Alligator gar harvest\r\n\r\nBoating and Water Safety:\r\n- Required safety equipment\r\n- Titling and registration requirements\r\n- Office locations\r\n- Operation of your boat\r\n\r\nLicenses and Certifications:\r\n- Connect and view your licenses and endorsements\r\n- Licenses, permits & stamps\r\n- License retailers near you\r\n- View hunter education certification\r\n- Purchase licenses online*\r\n\r\n*Some features require internet connection.\r\n\r\nIMPORTANT NOTICE: The information in this guide is a SUMMARY of the regulations and statutes governing hunting and fishing. For more detailed information on game and regulations, please contact a TPWD Law Enforcement office or call (800) 792-1112 (8 a.m. \u2013 5 p.m., Monday through Friday). Information contained in this summary is subject to change by the Texas Parks and Wildlife Commission, the Texas Legislature, and/or the federal government. The official regulations, current to the day, can be accessed at www.sos.state.tx.us under Title 31 of the Texas Administrative Code.",
    "descriptionHTML": "The Texas Outdoor Annual contains hunting, fishing, and boating regulations, all in one app.<br><br>Hunting:<br>- Hunting season dates &amp; limits for your county<br>- Seasons and bag limits for all game animals<br>- Means and methods restrictions<br>- Game tagging instructions<br>- Latest hunting news from TPWD*<br>- Links to report your hunt harvest<br><br>Fishing<br>- Statewide bag and length limits<br>- Exceptions to statewide limits by water body<br>- Places to fish nearby (over 1,000 locations)<br>- Fish identification<br>- Weekly fishing reports*<br>- Latest fishing news from TPWD*<br>- Links to report Alligator gar harvest<br><br>Boating and Water Safety:<br>- Required safety equipment<br>- Titling and registration requirements<br>- Office locations<br>- Operation of your boat<br><br>Licenses and Certifications:<br>- Connect and view your licenses and endorsements<br>- Licenses, permits &amp; stamps<br>- License retailers near you<br>- View hunter education certification<br>- Purchase licenses online*<br><br>*Some features require internet connection.<br><br>IMPORTANT NOTICE: The information in this guide is a SUMMARY of the regulations and statutes governing hunting and fishing. For more detailed information on game and regulations, please contact a TPWD Law Enforcement office or call (800) 792-1112 (8 a.m. \u2013 5 p.m., Monday through Friday). Information contained in this summary is subject to change by the Texas Parks and Wildlife Commission, the Texas Legislature, and/or the federal government. The official regulations, current to the day, can be accessed at www.sos.state.tx.us under Title 31 of the Texas Administrative Code.",
